@meta
id: 25-13
title: Drill — not column one
chapter: 25
type: drill
skills: ex-normal
par: 23
minutes: 4
reps: 8
vscode: click six lines one at a time and type the dash yourself
open: deploy-notes.md

@brief
Eight times: the six indented steps on lines 5 to 10 should be a bullet
list. Put `- ` in front of the text on each one. The indentation in front
of it stays exactly as it is.

`:normal` puts the cursor in **column 1** on each line, not on the first
non-blank. An `i` there types into the margin.

@keys
| `:5,10normal I- ` | insert `- ` at the first non-blank of each line |
| `I` | insert before the first non-blank character |
| `^` | move to the first non-blank character |

@hints
`i` inserts where the cursor is, and on these lines the cursor starts to
the left of the indentation. You want the key that goes to the text
first.
--
`:5,10normal I- ` Enter, `:wq`. Mind the space after the dash.

@solution
    :5,10normal I- <Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Twenty keystrokes. `:5,10normal ^i- ` is the same thing spelled out:
`^` to the first non-blank, then insert. `I` is that pair in one key, and
it is the one to reach for.

Column 1 is the single most common way a `:normal` goes wrong, and it is
the same trap as `:g//normal` from chapter 15 — same cause, same fix.
Anything that measures from the cursor is affected, not just insertion:
`dw` on an indented line eats the indentation instead of the first word,
`3x` takes three spaces, and `f(` starts its search from the margin,
which is usually what you wanted but not always.

The rule to carry: if the keys care where they start, start them with
`^`. It costs one keystroke and removes a whole class of surprise.

@start deploy-notes.md
# Payments release

Steps, in order:

  run the pending migration
  restart the payments worker
  drain the refund queue
  check the gateway dashboard
  watch the queue depth fall
  close the ticket

@expected deploy-notes.md
# Payments release

Steps, in order:

  - run the pending migration
  - restart the payments worker
  - drain the refund queue
  - check the gateway dashboard
  - watch the queue depth fall
  - close the ticket
